; The modus theme registers its file as the theme.
> (use-plugin modus)
> (tables:ref web:stylesheets 'theme #f)
"modus/modus.css"
; Its palette is Modus's: 109 named colours and 53 of Modus's mappings,
; each a pair of the operandi-tinted and the vivendi-tinted value.
> (length modus-colours)
162
> (malformed-modus-colours)
()
> (cdr (assoc "--modus-bg-main" modus-colours))
"light-dark(#fbf7f0, #0d0e1c)"
> (cdr (assoc "--modus-cursor" modus-colours))
"light-dark(#d00000, #ff66ff)"
; It sets every colour among the semantic tokens, faces' and seven
; components' colours, and reads only its own palette, Modus's two
; options and the bold weight. Docstrings, string escapes, directives
; such as #!tuna and library names take Modus's docstring, regexp
; backslash, preprocessor and type colours, as Emacs's Scheme faces do
; under Modus; variable definitions, uses, members and calls take its
; variable, variable-use, property and fnname-call colours, as Emacs's
; tree-sitter faces do.
> (list (length modus-mapping) (left-to-design-tokens) (unknown-in-theme) (unset-by-modus))
(134 () () ())
